### Summary of Security Guidelines
The security guidelines emphasize the importance of sanitizing user input to prevent XSS attacks, validating recipe IDs to avoid Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerabilities, and limiting input lengths to prevent excessive data storage. Specific measures include:
- Validating and escaping user inputs before rendering.
- Ensuring `recipeId` exists in the database before processing requests.
- Setting maximum length constraints on inputs (e.g., title: 255 characters, ingredients: 1000 characters total, comments: 500 characters).

